Project: Ceres Solver
URL: http://ceres-solver.org/
License: New BSD (LICENSE); include/ceres/internal/fixed_array.h and
include/ceres/internal/memory.h come from Abseil and are under the
Apache License 2.0 (also in LICENSE).
Upstream version: 2.2.0 (https://github.com/ceres-solver/ceres-solver/archive/refs/tags/2.2.0.tar.gz)

Natron builds it as upstream's CMake build would with
  -DMINIGLOG=ON -DSCHUR_SPECIALIZATIONS=OFF -DLAPACK=OFF -DSUITESPARSE=OFF
  -DEIGENSPARSE=OFF -DACCELERATESPARSE=OFF -DUSE_CUDA=OFF
that is, as the Ceres 1.11 that Natron bundled before: dense linear algebra
only, with Eigen (libs/Eigen3). Ceres' miniglog provides glog/logging.h, so
neither glog nor gflags is needed.

Local modifications: none. Files:
- include/ceres: the public headers, except manifold_test_utils.h (gtest).
- config/ceres/internal/config.h and export.h: written by hand, they replace
  the headers that upstream's CMake build generates (see their comments).
- internal/ceres: the library sources of upstream's
  internal/ceres/CMakeLists.txt (CERES_EXPORTED_SRCS, ceres_internal, the
  generated/*_d_d_d.cc Schur specializations, miniglog/glog/logging.cc), and
  the private headers they include.
- MAX_LOG_LEVEL=-2 (CMakeLists.txt, libs.pri): miniglog only prints errors.

To update: unpack the new release, copy the files listed above (the header
list can be made with "c++ -MM" on the sources), compare cmake/config.h.in
with config/ceres/internal/config.h, and update the file lists in
CMakeLists.txt and ceres.pro.
